@D KOSMOS_DIM_LADDER := "the KOSMOS anchor coordinate carries NEW independent info up to D*=6 (4 attribute-axes beyond 2D) then SATURATES — a finite axis capacity" :: discovery [d=2026-06-04 active]
  seed      = "PR #1765 added ONE axis (time, [x,y]->[x,y,t]) to the KOSMOS Psi-carving coordinate and found it captures carve-sequence, but flagged a near-tautology caveat: for monotone time encodings t is 1-1 with the carve-step so recovery partly reads back the encoding. Ladder the coordinate D=2->8 over the real anchor attributes (coord/lane/radius/tier/tags + time + modality) and ask the CAPACITY question #1765 did not: does each ADDED axis carry NEW independent info, or do axes SATURATE past some D*? Resolve the tautology by giving each axis its OWN independent latent class signal (noisy class-conditional embedding, NOT a shared monotone index) + two deliberately-injected redundancies (scale~time 0.85, lane~emotion 0.80) so redundancy is measurable."
  claim     = "On a STANDALONE toy (N=600 anchors, 3 seeds, CPU $0, kNN k=7 leave-one-out recovery of a held-out mixed-radix joint target), the dimension ladder shows a FINITE axis capacity D*=6. The 4 INDEPENDENT added axes each carry NEW info above their 2-SEM seed-noise band: t/time dAcc +0.003333+/-0.001361, e/emotion +0.008333+/-0.006804, tau/tier +0.011111+/-0.009061, m/modality +0.045556+/-0.012862 (largest single-axis). The 2 REDUNDANT axes SATURATE within noise: s/scale +0.018889+/-0.016906 (band 0.019521), kappa/lane +0.001111+/-0.005500 (band 0.006351). Per-axis shuffle confirms independence: own_drop (0.111..0.438) >> cross_drop (-0.0001..+0.034) for ALL 7 axes. Distance contrast 3.09(D=2)->1.94(D=8) > 1.0 -> NO collapse. The capacity knee D*=6 lands EXACTLY at the planted independent/redundant boundary."
  falsifier = "Pre-registered: a rung HOLDS only if dAcc(D) - 2*SEM > 0 (per-rung 2-standard-error-of-mean band over 3 seeds), SATURATED if within band, COLLAPSE if dAcc+2SEM<0; nothing rounded. NEW-INFO requires HOLD; PER-AXIS-SHUFFLE requires own_drop >> cross_drop; CAPACITY = max D with HOLDS; NO-COLLAPSE requires D=8 contrast > 1.0 and > 0.5x D=2. The redundant axes s and kappa FAILED the per-rung HOLD test (gain within 2-SEM band) -> recorded SATURATED, not rounded to HOLD (a_paper_negative_ok)."
  target    = "Per-rung: D=3/4/5/6 HOLDS (time/emotion/tier/modality), D=7/8 SATURATED (scale/lane). Capacity D*=6. The non-tautological evidence is the per-axis shuffle matrix (own_drop>>cross_drop) + the planted-redundancy recovery (D*=6 = injected boundary), NOT a monotone-index read-back."
  scope     = "TOY: deterministic toy independent-signal placement (noisy class-conditional Gaussian per axis), NOT the real conscious_decoder / 603MB s16 carve; injected redundancy (s~t, kappa~e) is a DESIGN CHOICE so saturation is measurable — the REAL KOSMOS anchor population's true cross-axis correlations are UNMEASURED. N=600, CPU/$0, STANDALONE (no wiring into engine_tensionlink_bench / clm_time_encoding / kosmos_io runtime). scale-transfer UNVERIFIED (a_toy_scale_recheck, a_scale_honest_scope, §97). Lane A/G split N/A (pure CPU toy)."
  honest    = "Capacity is REAL and FINITE — NO infinite-gain claim (a_paper_negative_ok: SATURATION at D*=6 IS the honest finding). This toy proves the METHOD and the capacity-curve SHAPE, not the real anchor set's true D*. The redundant axes still carry their OWN attribute (own_drop ~0.24-0.25) — their redundancy is that their attribute duplicates another axis's, which is why they add no NEW joint info yet shuffle-degrade their own. Resolves the #1765 monotone-index tautology caveat by independent class-conditional axes + per-axis shuffle control. No fabrication; verdicts verbatim (p7/g5)."
  note      = "harness UNIVERSE/kosmos_dim_ladder.py; verdicts .verdicts/kosmos-dim-ladder/{F-NEWINFO,F-PERAXIS-SHUFFLE,F-CAPACITY,F-NOCOLLAPSE,SUMMARY}.txt + results.json + run_stdout.txt (incremental-gain-per-D curve included). Modality (axis-6) carries the largest single-axis info — ties the real ingested modalities (EEG/LiDAR/dolphin-acoustic/text) as candidate KOSMOS coordinate axis-6. Continues PR #1765 (resolves its tautology caveat)."
